---
// Skills.astro
---
<section id="skills" class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto py-10 px-4">
  <div class="head">
    <h1
      class="bg-gradient-to-l from-secondary to-primary bg-clip-text text-transparent"
    >
      Skills & Tools
    </h1>
    <p class="space-y-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto text-lg font-medium text-center">
      <span class="block text-xl text-foreground">
        Tools change, but architectural principles endure. I select
        technologies based on stability, ecosystem maturity, and performance
        —never hype.
      </span>
      <span class="block text-muted mt-2">
        While I work comfortably across the full stack, my strongest
        contributions are in
        <strong class="text-foreground font-semibold"
          >database design and backend architecture
        </strong>
        —where system behavior, data integrity, and long-term scalability
        are decided.
      </span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto space-y-10 mt-12">
    <!-- Database Design -->
    <div class="db skill relative">
      <h4 class="title">Database Design</h4>

      <div class="desc">
        <p>
          I design databases as <strong>systems</strong>, not just storage
          layers.
        </p>

        <p>
          My focus is on data models that reflect real business constraints,
          enforcing
          <strong>integrity at the database level</strong>
          so data remains valid even if application code fails. I prioritize
          transaction boundaries, indexing strategies, and predictable query
          behavior under load.
        </p>

        <p>
          I work comfortably <strong>close to the metal</strong> —analyzing
          query plans, managing locking strategies, and writing raw
          SQL—while knowing exactly when to abstract complexity with an ORM.
          The goal is always the same: clear ownership, consistent
          performance, and schemas that can evolve without breaking
          production.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4">
          <span class="text-foreground font-montserrat font-semibold"
            >Core strengths:
          </span>
          <span class="block text-muted">
            Relational Modeling, Transactional Integrity, Indexing Strategy,
            Concurrency Control, Data Migrations.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="tools">
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/db.png"
            alt="SQL logo"
            class="img bg-cover bg-center size-6"
          />
          <p>SQL</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/postgres.png"
            alt="PostgreSQL logo"
            class="img bg-cover bg-center h-6 w-8"
          />
          <p>PostgreSQL</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/mysql.png"
            alt="MySQL logo"
            class="img object-cover size-6"
          />
          <p>MySQL</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/prisma.png"
            alt="Prisma ORM logo"
            class="img object-cover rounded-sm size-6"
          />
          <p>Prisma</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/redis.png"
            alt="Redis logo"
            class="img object-cover size-6 rounded-sm"
          />
          <p>Redis</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/mongodb.png"
            alt="mongoDb logo"
            class="img object-cover size-6"
          />
          <p>MongoDB</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/neon.jpeg"
            alt="Neon logo"
            class="img object-cover size-6"
          />
          <p>Neon</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Backend Engineering -->
    <div class="back-end skill relative">
      <h4 class="title">Backend Engineering</h4>

      <div>
        <div class="desc">
          <p>
            Backend engineering is my <strong>primary discipline</strong>.
          </p>

          <p>
            I build APIs and systems where
            <strong>business logic lives in isolated layers</strong>,
            independent of frameworks. This decoupling makes systems easier
            to test, reason about, and scale without being locked into
            specific tools.
          </p>

          <p>
            I pay strict attention to <strong>system boundaries</strong>:
            distinct separation between authentication and authorization,
            read vs. write models, and synchronous vs. asynchronous flows.
            Whether handling payments or modernizing legacy systems, I
            design backends to behave correctly under
            <strong>real-world conditions</strong> —handling failure states
            as gracefully as happy paths.
          </p>

          <p>
            This is my chosen specialization: designing robust,
            production-grade systems that businesses can rely on.
          </p>

          <p class="space-y-2 mt-4">
            <span class="text-foreground font-montserrat font-semibold"
              >Core strengths:
            </span>
            <span class="block text-muted">
              API Design, Authentication & Authorization, Transactional
              Workflows, System Architecture.
            </span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="flex gap-4 items-center my-6 p-3 px-4 text-base text-secondary bg-surface/50 border border-surface-border w-fit rounded-lg"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-gear"></i>
          <p class="font-mono font-semibold">RESTful API Design</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="tools">
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/typescript.png"
            alt="TypeScript logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>TypeScript</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/node.webp"
            alt="Node JS logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Node.js</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/express.webp"
            alt="Express JS logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Express</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/next.png"
            alt="Next JS logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Next.js</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/postman.png"
            alt="Postman logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Postman</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/cloudflare.png"
            alt="Cloudflare logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Cloudflare</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/vercel.png"
            alt="Vercel logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Vercel</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/netlify.png"
            alt="Netlify logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Netlify</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Frontend Engineering -->
    <div class="front-end skill relative">
      <h4 class="title">Frontend Engineering</h4>

      <div class="desc">
        <p>
          I approach frontend development with the same rigor as backend
          architecture.
        </p>

        <p>
          I specialize in <strong>data-dense interfaces</strong> —admin
          panels, dashboards, and internal tools —where clarity and
          precision are paramount. Users in these environments need to
          understand complex data and perform precise actions without
          fighting the UI.
        </p>

        <p>
          My focus is on <strong>state synchronization:</strong> robust data
          fetching patterns, correct error handling, and efficient cache
          invalidation. I design interactions where the UI is an accurate
          reflection of the backend state, ensuring responsiveness without
          becoming fragile. I build interfaces that users can
          <strong>trust</strong>.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4">
          <span class="text-foreground font-montserrat font-semibold"
            >Core strengths:
          </span>
          <span class="block text-muted">
            Data-Heavy UI Design, Admin Dashboards, Structured Layouts,
            Predictable State Management, Clean and Maintainable Front-end
            Architecture.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="tools">
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/typescript.png"
            alt="TypeScript logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>TypeScript</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/next.png"
            alt="Next JS logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Next.js</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/react.png"
            alt="React JS logo"
            class="img h-5 w-6"
          />
          <p>React.js</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/tailwind.png"
            alt="Tailwind logo"
            class="img h-4 w-6"
          />
          <p>Tailwind</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/tanstack-query.png"
            alt="TanStack Query logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Tanstack Query</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/redux.png" alt="Redux logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>Redux</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/zod.png" alt="Zod logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>Zod</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/gsap.png" alt="GSAP logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>GSAP</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/motion.png"
            alt="Framer Motion logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Motion</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Dev Tools -->
    <div class="global pt-8">
      <h3 class="text-2xl py-4 font-iceberg font-semibold text-primary">
        Dev Tools:
      </h3>
      <ul class="tools flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center justify-start">
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/git.png" alt="Git logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>Git</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <i class="fa-brands fa-github text-2xl"></i>
          <p>GitHub</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/bash.png" alt="Bash logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>Linux / Bash</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/npm.png" alt="npm logo" class="img h-4 w-6" />
          <p>NPM</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img src="/logos/pnpm.webp" alt="pnpm logo" class="img size-6" />
          <p>PNPM</p>
        </li>
        <li class="tool">
          <img
            src="/logos/gemini.png"
            alt="Gemini AI logo"
            class="img size-6"
          />
          <p>Gemini</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
